------------------------------------------------------------\par
1. BUSINESS CONTEXT\par
------------------------------------------------------------\par
\par
NexaMart is a fictional multi-category retail company\par
operating across multiple regions and sales channels.\par
\par
Management wants to better understand revenue performance,\par
customer value, product profitability, regional performance,\par
sales channel performance, and the impact of discounts on\par
profitability.\par
\par
The project is designed to simulate a realistic retail\par
business environment and demonstrate how transactional data\par
can be transformed into actionable business intelligence.\par
\par
\par
------------------------------------------------------------\par
2. BUSINESS PROBLEM\par
------------------------------------------------------------\par
\par
Revenue growth does not necessarily translate into\par
proportional profit growth.\par
\par
Management therefore requires a data-driven analytical\par
framework to understand the drivers of revenue and\par
profitability across customers, products, categories,\par
regions, and sales channels.\par
\par
The analysis aims to answer the following questions:\par
\par
1. Which products generate the most revenue and profit?\par
\par
2. Which products and categories have weak profitability?\par
\par
3. Which customers contribute the most value?\par
\par
4. Which customer segments are the most profitable?\par
\par
5. Which regions perform best and worst?\par
\par
6. Which sales channels are most profitable?\par
\par
7. How do discounts affect profitability and margins?\par
\par
8. Where are the biggest opportunities for improving profit?\f0\par
\par
\par
\par
\par
\b0\fs22 ------------------------------------------------------------\par
3. PROJECT OBJECTIVE\par
------------------------------------------------------------\par
\par
Build an end-to-end analytics solution using Python, SQL,\par
Excel, and Power BI to analyse sales, customers, products,\par
regions, sales channels, and profitability.\par
\par
The project aims to transform transactional data into\par
actionable business insights and management recommendations.\par
\par
