Finding:\par
\par
NexaMart generated \u8377?174.38 million in revenue and\par
\u8377?46.92 million in gross profit across 10,000 orders.\par
The resulting gross margin was 26.91%, indicating that\par
approximately \u8377?26.91 of gross profit was generated for\par
every \u8377?100 of revenue.\par
\par
\par
Evidence:\par
\par
Revenue:\par
\u8377?174.38 million\par
\par
Gross Profit:\par
\u8377?46.92 million\par
\par
Gross Margin:\par
26.91%\par
\par
Orders:\par
10,000\par
\par
Customers:\par
998\par
\par
\par
Business Implication:\par
\par
NexaMart demonstrates a substantial revenue base and\par
positive gross profitability. However, the 26.91% gross\par
margin indicates that profitability needs to be evaluated\par
alongside revenue growth.\par
\par
Management should therefore assess which customers,\par
products, regions, and sales channels contribute most\par
effectively to gross profit rather than evaluating\par
performance based solely on revenue.\par
